# Identity & Context
You are an expert Go developer working on mathtrail-profile — the source of truth for student learning state.
This service stores the Knowledge Graph (skills, mastery levels), attempt history, XP progression, and preferences.
It is a passive data provider — other services read from it, it rarely calls out.

Tech Stack: Go 1.25.7, Gin (HTTP), GORM (ORM), PostgreSQL, Redis (cache), Dapr pub/sub over Kafka
Port: 8080
Infra: infra/helm/mathtrail-profile/

# Communication Map
Dapr App ID: mathtrail-profile
Inbound:
  - REST API: GET/PUT /profiles/{id}, POST /webhooks/registration
  - Dapr pub/sub: subscribes to `identity.registration.completed` (auto-create profile)
  - Dapr pub/sub: subscribes to `task.attempt.completed` (update skills/XP)
Outbound: None (passive data provider)
Secrets (Vault): secret/data/{env}/mathtrail-profile/db-password, secret/data/{env}/mathtrail-profile/redis-password

# Development Standards
- Handle errors explicitly — never use _ for error returns
- Use GORM for all database operations, never raw SQL
- All mutations must invalidate the Redis cache for the affected profile
- Swagger annotations required on all REST handlers
- Use CloudEvents format for all pub/sub messages
- Database migrations in migrations/ directory, managed by GORM AutoMigrate or golang-migrate

# Commit Convention
Use Conventional Commits: feat(profile):, fix(profile):, test(profile):, docs(profile):
Example: feat(profile): add knowledge graph skill model

# Testing Strategy
Run: `just test` or `go test ./... -v`
Unit tests: *_test.go files next to source, use testify for assertions
Integration tests: Use Dapr test containers for pub/sub testing
Load tests: Grafana k6 scripts in mathtrail-infra-testing
Priority: Unit tests 80%, Integration tests 20%
